          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>You are correct. The problem is that neural impulses are not supposed to start there!</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>You should have chosen this answer. It happens in wind up even though neural impulses are not supposed to start there.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Inflammation of the dorsal root ganglion, resulting in initiation of neural impulses&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Yes, and if the longer lasting neurotransmitter is being used to transmit pain, the pain lasts longer.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>This is one of the correct answers, and the result is that the pain lasts longer.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Increased use of the neurotransmitter glutamate that has a longer half life than the other neurotransmitter, substance p</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Fewer inhibitory signals and fewer inhibitory neurons in the \"gate\", which is the area between the first and second order of neurons.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Actually, serotonin and noradrenaline are inhibitory neurons at the gate, and we WANT more of those there to decrease the pain.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Correct,&nbsp;serotonin and noradrenaline are inhibitory neurons at the gate, and we WANT more of those there to decrease the pain.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Increased serotonin and noradrenaline in the area of the 'gate'</div>\n"
                }
              ],
